From fe265cdc2a13c015c4db22b32080138fd25163d4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 16:17:06 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] fix(xtask): heavy wave record never passes a partial run;
 owed heavy result

Review fixes on #3470:
- `--covers` refuses `--only` and `--failed`; the record has the planned
  step count beside the run count, and its verdict is INCOMPLETE when a
  planned step did not run, NO LANE when the wave reaches no heavy lane.
- The header, the summary and covers.txt name the base (the merge base
  of HEAD and --base). The merge-ready skill runs the planner again when
  main moved after the run.
- A wave-2 PR keeps its heavy result through a SAME or MECHANICAL
  refresh; DELTA or NEW CODE needs a new result.
- `<!-- heavy-wave: ... -->` joins the fixed strings and the
  collaborator-marker rule in AGENTS.md.

The maintainer's decision on #3467: a review of a P3 or lower PR can set
merge-ready with "not run - owed to the wave run before merge"; the merge
waits for a record that names the final head. P1 and P2 keep the strict
rule. Pinned by an_owed_heavy_result_is_allowed_for_p3_and_lower_only.

Fixes #3460
Fixes #3467

